# Runtime environment for every benchmark and gate invocation.
#
# Forwarded by `evo env load`, so it applies without editing bench/run --
# which is hash-pinned in .evo/harness.lock and should not move for this.
#
# WHY: avoid_ms is measured with time.process_time() (sim2d.py:167), which
# sums CPU across ALL THREADS of the process. numpy/OpenBLAS keeps a spinning
# thread pool, and whenever its spin window overlapped a timed plan() call
# that spin time was charged straight into the candidate's score.
#
# process_time() is the right clock and is deliberately kept: it is
# thread-count neutral, so a candidate that uses several threads is charged
# their total CPU and gains nothing for free. The bug was never the clock --
# it was the referee's OWN threads being counted as the candidate's work.
#
# Measured, exp_0008's committed binary, 6 alternating battery runs:
#   default   speed 0.8291 / 0.8015 / 0.7957   fitness spread 0.334
#   threads=1 speed 0.9987 / 0.9994 / 0.9994   fitness spread 0.0069
# gold and consistency were bit-identical in all six, so the entire effect
# was the clock. Note calibration_ms ran BACKWARDS across the default runs,
# which rules out ambient machine load as the explanation.
OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1
OMP_NUM_THREADS=1
MKL_NUM_THREADS=1
NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=1
VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=1
